# Commit identity (mandatory)

This repository is public. Commit identity is a security boundary.

## Required identity

Every `git commit` in this repo MUST use:

- Name: `Podwarack`
- Email: `328382584+podwarack@users.noreply.github.com`

Do this by exporting those values as `GIT_AUTHOR_*` and `GIT_COMMITTER_*`
and by passing:

`git -c user.name=Podwarack -c user.email=328382584+podwarack@users.noreply.github.com`

Do not use the machine's default `user.name` / `user.email`.
Do not use a personal legal name, a local hostname email, or `cursoragent`.

## Forbidden trailers

NEVER add, keep, or restore:

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor`
- `Co-authored-by: cursoragent`
- `--trailer` / `--footer` values that mention Cursor
- "Made with Cursor" in commit messages or PR bodies

If Cursor injects a trailer, strip it before the commit is pushed.

## After every commit

Verify before push:

```bash
git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>%n%cn <%ce>%n%B'
```

Author and committer must both be Podwarack. The body must not contain
`Co-authored-by` or `Cursor`.

If either check fails, amend immediately with the Podwarack identity
and a cleaned message, then verify again.
